Chapter: ActTailRt

 The input shape the corpus lacked. Every recursion in deep-recursion-rt
 tails through an `if` or a `let`; none tails through an `act`, and the
 tail-call walker had no arm for one, so a call in the last statement of an
 act block was emitted as an ordinary call. That is the shape
 emit-streaming-ir-defs is written in, which is why the compiler's own
 self-compile grew a frame per definition and died 4,805 definitions deep
 inside a browser worker while every subject here stayed green.

 The stack is pinned to a browser worker's megabyte by the sidecar, and the
 depths are far past what that many real frames would fit, so a plug that
 emits an ordinary call cannot pass this chapter.

  loop-act : Integer, Integer -> [Console] Integer
  loop-act (i) (len) =
   if i == len then i
   else act
    let step = i + 1
    in loop-act step len
   end

  ping-act : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  ping-act (n) =
   if n <= 0 then 0
   else act
    let m = n - 1
    in pong-act m
   end

  pong-act : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  pong-act (n) =
   if n <= 0 then 1
   else act
    let m = n - 1
    in ping-act m
   end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   r <- loop-act 0 300000
   print-line-uni (show r)
   p <- ping-act 300000
   print-line-uni (show p)
   q <- pong-act 300001
   print-line-uni (show q)
  end
